# Apex Drive — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local (or set in the deploy environment) and re-run `bun run publish`.

# NOTE: All business content (company name, location, hours, phone, Telegram
# handle, hero copy, and the default vehicle catalog) now lives in ONE file:
#   config/siteConfig.ts
# To create a new client site, edit that file — there is no env var for it.

# Supabase — OPTIONAL for the public site. When both are set, the site fetches
# from the `vehicles` table (see supabase/schema.sql); otherwise it falls back to
# the seeded catalog in siteConfig. The site never crashes on a missing/broken
# Supabase config.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Admin dashboard passcode (server-only — read at request time, NEVER shipped
# to the client, never a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var). Required for /admin: without it the
# login page refuses access. Set a strong value in production and re-publish.
# The local sandbox demo uses a gitignored .env.local (see the lead's report for
# the demo value) — do not commit real passcodes.
# ADMIN_PASSCODE=
